description', 'get_prompt', 'icons', 'instructions', 'list_prompts', 'list_resource_templates', 'list_resources', 'list_tools', 'middleware', 'name', 'prompt', 'read_resource', 'remove_prompt', 'remove_tool', 'resource', 'run', 'run_sse_async', 'run_stdio_async', 'run_streamable_http_async', 'session_manager', 'sse_app', 'streamable_http_app', 'title', 'tool', 'version', 'website_url']\n\n/Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-tfe1ts5p/retort-a725f4ae3f5d/venv/lib/python3.12/site-packages/mcp/server/mcpserver/__init__.py\n","exit":0,"truncated":false},"title":"source venv/bin/activate && python -c \"\nfrom mcp.server.mcpserver import MCPServer\nimport inspect\nsig = inspect.signature(MCPServer.__init__)\nprint('MCPServer init:', sig)\nprint([m for m in dir(MCPServer) if not m.startswith('_')])\nprint()\nimport mcp.server.mcpserver as m\nprint(inspect.getsourcefile(m))\n\"","time":{"start":1788280456129,"end":1788280456173}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"Interesting. The `mcp` 2.x renamed `FastMCP` to `MCPServer` in `mcp.server.mcpserver`. Let me check the new API.\n\nTeam names across files:\n- Brasileirao: \"Flamengo-RJ\" (with state suffix, unaccented: \"Atletico-GO\", \"Avai-SC\", \"Ceara-CE\")\n- novo: \"Flamengo\", \"América-MG\" (accented with state)\n- BR-Football: \"Flamengo\", \"Athletico Paranaense\" (spelled out, no accents)\n- Copa do Brasil: \"Flamengo - RJ\"? Let me check. Sample shows \"America - MG\" — with \" - \" separator.\n- Libertadores: \"Nacional (URU)\", \"Barcelona-EQU\" etc.\n\nSo normalization: strip state suffixes (e.g. \"-RJ\", \" - RJ\"), remove accents, lowercase, remove punctuation, and also handle \"Athletico Paranaense\" vs \"Atlético-PR\"? Hmm — \"Athletico Paranaense\" (BR-Football) vs \"Athletico-PR\" (novo) vs \"Atletico-PR\" (Brasileirao unaccented). Note Athletico-PR and Atlético-PR... Actually the same club is \"Athletico Paranaense\" (formerly Atlético-PR, renamed in 2019). The datasets use both spellings. This is a hard matching problem in general.\n\nI need a normalization approach:\n1. Unicode NFKD, strip accents\n2. lowercase\n3. remove state suffix patterns: trailing \"-XX\" or \" - XX\" or \"(XX)\" where XX is a Brazilian state UF (2 letters)\n4. remove punctuation, collapse whitespace\n5. Also expand/strip common suffixes like \"EC\", \"FC\", \"Sport Club\", \"Esporte Clube\"? Maybe minimal: handle alias mapping for common variants.\n\nAlso fuzzy matching might be needed (\"Athletico Paranaense\" -> \"athletico paranaense\" vs \"atletico pr\" -> \"atletico\"). Hmm, that won't match with pure normalization. Let me think about what's needed for the required behaviors:\n\n- \"Show me all Flamengo vs Fluminense matches\" — Flamengo appears as \"Flamengo-RJ\" (Brasileirao), \"Flamengo\" (novo, BR-Football), \"Flamengo - RJ\"? Let me check Copa do Brasil. Base normalization handles these.\n- \"Which players play for Flamengo?\" — FIFA data uses \"Flamengo\" probably. Let me check the club names in fifa_data.\n\nFor robustness I'll add:\n- A canonical alias table for well-known Brazilian clubs mapping variants to a canonical key (e.g., \"atletico pr\" / \"athletico paranaense\" / \"athletico\" -> \"athletico-paranaense\"). Actually, let me be careful: it's better to have a curated alias map for major clubs plus generic normalization.\n\nLet me check the FIFA club names for Brazilian clubs.\n\nAlso check the MCPServer API in mcp 2.x.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_05dd2405800194zopm6tpWvm0w","sessionID":"ses_fa22e85f8ffeHYTJ3TNp22RZ2x","messageID":"msg_05dd22555001zt9yFto5RpWhHR"}}
