{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788280587743,"sessionID":"ses_fa22e85f8ffeHYTJ3TNp22RZ2x","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"bash","callID":"chatcmpl-tool-9eb5d1d8832983c7","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"python3 << 'EOF'\nimport csv\nfrom collections import Counter\ndef load(f):\n    with open(f, encoding='utf-8') as fh:\n        return list(csv.DictReader(fh))\nb = load('data/kaggle/Brasileirao_Matches.csv')\nbr = load('data/kaggle/BR-Football-Dataset.csv')\n\ndef norm(t):  # strip state suffix\n    return t.split('-')[0].strip() if '-SP' in t or '-RJ' in t or '-MG' in t or '-PR' in t or '-SC' in t or '-RS' in t or '-GO' in t or '-CE' in t or '-BA' in t or '-PE' in t or '-MT' in t or '-AL' in t or '-RN' in t or '-ES' in t or '-PB' in t or '-PI' in t or '-MS' in t or '-DF' in t or '-TO' in t or '-SE' in t or '-PA' in t or '-AM' in t or '-AP' in t or '-RO' in t or '-MA' in t else t\n\nf1 = Counter()\ndates1 = {}\nfor r in b:\n    if r['season']=='2019' and ('Flamengo' in r['home_team'] or 'Flamengo' in r['away_team']):\n        h, a = norm(r['home_team']), norm(r['away_team'])\n        hg, ag = int(r['home_goal']), int(r['away_goal'])\n        f1[(h, a, hg, ag)] += 1\n        dates1[(h,a,hg,ag)] = r['datetime'][:10]\nf2 = Counter()\ndates2 = {}\nfor r in br:\n    if r['tournament']=='Serie A' and r['date'].startswith('2019') and r['home']=='Flamengo' or (r['tournament']=='Serie A' and r['date'].startswith('2019') and r['away']=='Flamengo'):\n        h, a = r['home'], r['away']\n        hg, ag = int(float(r['home_goal'])), int(float(r['away_goal']))\n        f2[(h, a, hg, ag)] += 1\n        dates2[(h,a,hg,ag)] = r['date']\n\nprint('b fixtures:', sum(f1.values()), 'br fixtures:', sum(f2.values()))\ninter = (f1 & f2)\nprint('same fixture+score:', sum(inter.values()))\nprint('date agreement among common:', sum(1 for k in inter if dates1[k]==dates2[k]), '/', len(inter))\nprint('only in b:', list((f1-f2).elements())[:6])\nprint('only in br:', list((f2-f1).elements())[:6])\nEOF","workdir":"/Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-tfe1ts5p/retort-a725f4ae3f5d"},"output":"b fixtures: 38 br fixtures: 38\nsame fixture+score: 24\ndate agreement among common: 21 / 24\nonly in b: [('Atletico', 'Flamengo', 2, 1), ('Flamengo', 'Atletico', 3, 2), ('Flamengo', 'Fortaleza', 2, 0), ('Csa', 'Flamengo', 0, 2), ('Flamengo', 'Botafogo', 3, 2), ('Bahia', 'Flamengo', 3, 0)]\nonly in br: [('Flamengo', 'Vasco Da Gama RJ', 4, 4), ('Flamengo', 'EC Bahia', 3, 1), ('Botafogo RJ', 'Flamengo', 0, 1), ('Flamengo', 'CSA', 1, 0), ('Fortaleza FC', 'Flamengo', 1, 2), ('Athletico Paranaense', 'Flamengo', 0, 2)]\n","metadata":{"output":"b fixtures: 38 br fixtures: 38\nsame fixture+score: 24\ndate agreement among common: 21 / 24\nonly in b: [('Atletico', 'Flamengo', 2, 1), ('Flamengo', 'Atletico', 3, 2), ('Flamengo', 'Fortaleza', 2, 0), ('Csa', 'Flamengo', 0, 2), ('Flamengo', 'Botafogo', 3, 2), ('Bahia', 'Flamengo', 3, 0)]\nonly in br: [('Flamengo', 'Vasco Da Gama RJ', 4, 4), ('Flamengo', 'EC Bahia', 3, 1), ('Botafogo RJ', 'Flamengo', 0, 1), ('Flamengo', 'CSA', 1, 0), ('Fortaleza FC', 'Flamengo', 1, 2), ('Athletico Paranaense', 'Flamengo', 0, 2)]\n","exit":0,"truncated":false},"title":"python3 << 'EOF'\nimport csv\nfrom collections import Counter\ndef load(f):\n    with open(f, encoding='utf-8') as fh:\n        return list(csv.DictReader(fh))\nb = load('data/kaggle/Brasileirao_Matches.csv')\nbr = load('data/kaggle/BR-Football-Dataset.csv')\n\ndef norm(t):  # strip state suffix\n    return t.split('-')[0].strip() if '-SP' in t or '-RJ' in t or '-MG' in t or '-PR' in t or '-SC' in t or '-RS' in t or '-GO' in t or '-CE' in t or '-BA' in t or '-PE' in t or '-MT' in t or '-AL' in t or '-RN' in t or '-ES' in t or '-PB' in t or '-PI' in t or '-MS' in t or '-DF' in t or '-TO' in t or '-SE' in t or '-PA' in t or '-AM' in t or '-AP' in t or '-RO' in t or '-MA' in t else t\n\nf1 = Counter()\ndates1 = {}\nfor r in b:\n    if r['season']=='2019' and ('Flamengo' in r['home_team'] or 'Flamengo' in r['away_team']):\n        h, a = norm(r['home_team']), norm(r['away_team'])\n        hg, ag = int(r['home_goal']), int(r['away_goal'])\n        f1[(h, a, hg, ag)] += 1\n        dates1[(h,a,hg,ag)] = r['datetime'][:10]\nf2 = Counter()\ndates2 = {}\nfor r in br:\n    if r['tournament']=='Serie A' and r['date'].startswith('2019') and r['home']=='Flamengo' or (r['tournament']=='Serie A' and r['date'].startswith('2019') and r['away']=='Flamengo'):\n        h, a = r['home'], r['away']\n        hg, ag = int(float(r['home_goal'])), int(float(r['away_goal']))\n        f2[(h, a, hg, ag)] += 1\n        dates2[(h,a,hg,ag)] = r['date']\n\nprint('b fixtures:', sum(f1.values()), 'br fixtures:', sum(f2.values()))\ninter = (f1 & f2)\nprint('same fixture+score:', sum(inter.values()))\nprint('date agreement among common:', sum(1 for k in inter if dates1[k]==dates2[k]), '/', len(inter))\nprint('only in b:', list((f1-f2).elements())[:6])\nprint('only in br:', list((f2-f1).elements())[:6])\nEOF","time":{"start":1788280587737,"end":1788280587742}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"Whoa: \"in b not br: []\" — every 2019 Flamengo fixture+score in Brasileirao_Matches also exists in BR-Football (fixture+score matched), but \"in br not b\" has entries — meaning BR-Football has EXTRA Flamengo 2019 matches not in Brasileirao file?? Wait, (f1 - f2) empty means b's fixtures ⊆ br's fixtures. (f2 - f1) non-empty means br has 19-ish fixtures... wait but same fixture+score count is 0?! That's contradictory. Oh I see — the (f1 & f2) intersection is 0 but f1 - f2 is empty... that can't be. Unless f1 is empty! Let me think: f1 counts matches where 'Flamengo' in home/away. I split team names by '-' and take [0] — \"Vasco da Gama-RJ\".split('-')[0] = 'Vasca da Gama'?? No wait — \"Vasco da Gama-RJ\" has no hyphen... it's \"Vasco da Gama-RJ\" — split('-') gives ['Vasco da Gama', 'RJ']? No! \"Vasco da Gama-RJ\" — hmm, there's a hyphen only before RJ: \"Vasco da Gama-RJ\".split('-') = ['Vasco da Gama', 'RJ']. OK that's fine.\n\nHmm wait, why would (f1 & f2) be 0 while f1 - f2 empty? If f1 is nonempty and f1 - f2 is empty, then f1 ⊆ f2, so f1 & f2 = f1 ≠ 0. Unless... f1 is empty! Let me recheck: 'Flamengo' in (r['home_team'], r['away_team']) — home_team is 'Flamengo-RJ', so 'Flamengo' in ('Flamengo-RJ', ...) is True (substring 'in' on tuple checks membership, not substring! Wait no — 'Flamengo' in ('Flamengo-RJ', 'Cruzeiro-MG') checks if 'Flamengo' equals any element — it does NOT do substring matching. 'Flamengo' != 'Flamengo-RJ'. So f1 is EMPTY!\n\nHa, my bug in the exploration script (not in the data). f1 empty → \"in b not br: []\" trivially, \"in br not b\" = all br matches. So the real question remains: do fixtures agree across files? Let me redo with proper matching.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_05dd43b230016yUBDdFlPUq4ZP","sessionID":"ses_fa22e85f8ffeHYTJ3TNp22RZ2x","messageID":"msg_05dd421a80011fVsCXzqp7qYUk"}}
