Mineiro', '1.0', '1.0')\n('2021-02-04', 'EC Bahia', 'Fluminense', '0.0', '1.0')\n('2021-02-21', 'Fortaleza FC', 'EC Bahia', '0.0', '4.0')\n('2021-12-05', 'EC Bahia', 'Fluminense', '2.0', '0.0')\n('2021-12-10', 'Fortaleza FC', 'EC Bahia', '2.0', '1.0')\n('2021-12-10', 'Gremio', 'Atletico Mineiro', '4.0', '3.0')\n","exit":0,"truncated":false},"title":"python3 << 'EOF'\nimport csv\nfrom collections import Counter\ndef load(f):\n    with open(f, encoding='utf-8') as fh:\n        return list(csv.DictReader(fh))\nbr = load('data/kaggle/BR-Football-Dataset.csv')\n# 2021 Serie A: count fixture pairs\nc = Counter()\nfor r in br:\n    if r['tournament']=='Serie A' and r['date'][:4]=='2021':\n        c[(r['home'], r['away'])] += 1\ndups = {k: v for k, v in c.items() if v > 1}\nprint('2021 Serie A pairs appearing >1:', len(dups), 'total matches:', sum(c.values()))\nprint(list(dups.items())[:5])\n# check if duplicated pairs have different scores/dates\nrows = [(r['date'], r['home'], r['away'], r['home_goal'], r['away_goal']) for r in br if r['tournament']=='Serie A' and r['date'][:4]=='2021' and (r['home'], r['away']) in list(dups)[:3]]\nfor x in sorted(rows): print(x)\nEOF","time":{"start":1788280597718,"end":1788280597722}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"Now clear: the two files describe the same 2019 Flamengo season; 24 fixtures match by (teams, score) — the remaining differences are purely naming (\"Csa\" vs \"CSA\", \"Bahia\" vs \"EC Bahia\", \"Fortaleza\" vs \"Fortaleza FC\", \"Atletico\" vs \"Athletico Paranaense\", \"Vasco da Gama-RJ\" vs \"Vasco Da Gama RJ\"). Date agreement 21/24 for common ones (3 date discrepancies — BR-Football has some inaccurate dates; e.g. my earlier date comparison was bugged).\n\nSo: BR-Football Serie A largely duplicates Brasileirao_Matches (2014-2022 overlap) with inferior team naming and slightly different/sometimes-wrong dates. And it extends to 2023 (which Brasileirao_Matches lacks). Plus Serie B, Serie C, and extra stats (corners, shots, attacks).\n\nDedup strategy: BR-Football Serie A matches duplicate Brasileirao matches. For standings 2014-2022, using both would double count. I need dedup. Key by (competition, season, home_canon, away_canon) — each fixture played exactly once per season in league play (home/away legs are separate fixtures). BR-Football Serie A 2021 has 491 matches vs 380 in Brasileirao — extra 111?? Serie A 2021 should be 380. 491 includes... hmm. Let me check what the extra 111 are. Maybe duplicated fixtures with different dates?! If BR-Football contains the same fixture twice with different dates and scores, then (competition, season, home, away) key would dedup within BR-Football too — keeping the first. Risky but let me check.\n\nAlso for Copa do Brasil: Brazilian_Cup_Matches 2012-2021 vs BR-Football 'Copa do Brasil' 2014-2023 — two-legged ties mean same fixture pairs appear twice per season legitimately (home/away legs) — dedup by (competition, season, home, away) would WRONGLY merge the two legs if dates differ... no wait, two legs have different home/away orientations usually (leg 1 at A's home, leg 2 at B's home) — (home, away) pairs differ. But sometimes both legs at same venue? Rare. Hmm, also Copa do Brasil single-match early rounds with draws decided by... whatever, scores recorded.\n\nActually safer dedup key: (competition, season, date, home_canon, away_canon). If two files disagree on the date of the same fixture (21/24 agree, 3 don't), the same match appears twice with different dates. That double-counts in h2h. Hmm.\n\nAlternative: dedup on (competition, season, home, away) for LEAGUE competitions only (Série A/B/C — each fixture pair meets exactly once at each venue per season), and for CUPS dedup on (competition, season, date, home, away) plus score match... For cups, same pair can meet twice (two legs, swapped venues) or even same venue twice (final at Maracanã etc.). Hmm.\n\nLet me quantify: how many exact duplicates (competition, season, date, home, away, score) exist across files after canonicalization? And how many (comp, season, home, away) pairs appear twice in BR-Football alone? Let me check the 2021 Serie A 491 anomaly.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_05dd4681e001j0MJoTZSBKHzby","sessionID":"ses_fa22e85f8ffeHYTJ3TNp22RZ2x","messageID":"msg_05dd44738001lvFoiaXpBuSD8Z"}}
