asemiro).\n- Copa do Brasil round 8 = final (two legs: e.g. 2013 Flamengo champion... 2013 final was Flamengo vs Athletico-PR — Flamengo won 2-0 second leg. Data shows exactly that).\n- Libertadores 2019 final: Flamengo 2-1 River Plate ✓. 2020 final Palmeiras 1-0 Santos ✓. There's a season 'NA' row with goals '-' — 2021 final (Flamengo vs Athletico-PR, Palmeiras?) Actually 2021 final was Flamengo 2-1 Athletico-PR? Hmm no — 2021 Libertadores final: Flamengo vs Athletico-PR? No wait, 2021 final was Flamengo... Actually 2021 winner was Flamengo (beat Athletico-PR? no — beaten Palmeiras? The 2021 final was Flamengo 2-1 Athletico... hmm I don't remember precisely. The row shows season NA, Flamengo vs Athletico, goals '-'. That's 2021 final (Flamengo won 2-1). The row is damaged (season NA, goals '-'). I must handle: season NA -> None, goals '-' -> None. My match queries must not crash on these.\n\nNote Libertadores 'Athletico' bare = Athletico-PR (alias needed) ✓ (already noted).\n\nCopa do Brasil team names: 'Atlético Paranaense - PR', 'Flamengo - RJ', 'Santos - SP' — \" - \" separator with accents. My normalizer handles: strip accents -> 'atletico paranaense pr' -> alias 'atletico paranaense' -> atletico-pr ✓. 'Flamengo - RJ' -> 'flamengo rj' -> alias -> flamengo ✓.\n\nNow — FIFA19 players at Brazilian clubs: Grêmio 20 Brazilian players etc. The spec example \"Who are the highest-rated players at Flamengo?\" — Flamengo not in FIFA data. But 'Santos', 'Grêmio' etc. are. Tests will use Santos/Grêmio.\n\nWait — one more check on FIFA clubs: 'Santos' = Santos-SP (Brazilian). Also 'Santos Laguna' Mexican. Alias 'santos' -> santos. ✓\n\nNow, country tags in Libertadores: 'Barcelona-EQU', 'Nacional (URU)', 'Nacional-URU', 'Guaraní (PAR)', 'Guaraní-PAR', 'Libertad-PAR', 'Olimpia-PAR', 'River Plate-URU', 'Delfín-EQU', 'Trujillanos (VEN)', 'Universitario (PER)', 'Universitario-PER', 'Mineros de Guaiana' (VEN)... So tag forms: '-XXX' and '(XXX)' with 3-letter codes mostly. I'll detect trailing token of 2-3 uppercase letters (in tag set) as country tag. List of country tags seen: URU, PAR, EQU, PER, VEN, ARG?, BOL?, CHI?, COL?, ECU? Let me extract all tags from Libertadores names to build the set. Also note: 'Athletico' bare (BR), 'Real Atlético'... hmm 'Real Atlético'? That's weird — probably Real Garcilaso? Whatever.\n\nAlso careful: 2-letter UF detection could misfire on foreign names ending in UF-like tokens... e.g. 'CSA - AL' fine. 'América de Cali' — 'Cali' isn't UF. OK.\n\nOne more consideration — 'Guaraní (PAR)' vs 'Guaraní-PAR': both normalize to 'guarani-par' ✓ same club. But bare 'Guaraní' (PAR club)? Not present I think. 'Libertad' bare AND 'Libertad-PAR' both present! Need alias: 'libertad par' -> 'libertad'. And 'Tolima' vs 'Deportes Tolima' — both present, same club (Colombia). Alias 'deportes tolima' -> 'tolima'. 'Independiente Del Valle' vs 'Independiente del Valle' — same (case). Fine after lowercase. 'Junior de Barranquilla' vs 'Junior'? Only 'Junior de Barranquilla' listed. OK.\n\nLet me extract all Libertadores tags + check 'Athletico'/'Real Atlético' weirdness. Then write the code.\n\nActually, let me also grab biggest wins data quickly for test assertions (compute after building the real module — better to write the implementation first, then explore with it, then finalize tests).\n\nTime to write the implementation. Structure:\n\n```\nbrazilian_soccer_mcp/\n  __init__.py\n  models.py\n  normalize.py\n  loader.py\n  service.py\n  server.py\n  __main__.py\ntests/ (conftest + 7 test modules)\nrequirements.txt\n```\n\nLet me now write each file carefully.\n\n### normalize.py details\n\n```python\nCLUBS: dict[canonical_id, (display_name, [aliases])]\n```\n\nLet me define the major club table (canonical_id -> display, aliases normalized):\n\nBrazilian clubs (Série A relevant 2003-2023):\n- flamengo: Flamengo; aliases: flamengo, flamengo rj, flamengo-rj → normalized 'flamengo rj'\n- fluminense: Fluminense; fluminense, flumin