right for unique clubs, wrong for ambiguous ones.\n\nSolution: generic rule = strip trailing UF, UNLESS the stripped base is in the AMBIGUOUS set {botafogo, america, vitoria, santos, atletico, nacional, guarani, internacional?...}. When base ∈ AMBIGUOUS and tag present → keep id as base-tag. When base ∈ AMBIGUOUS and no tag → map via DEFAULT_ALIAS (botafogo→botafogo-rj, santos→santos, america→america-mg, vitoria→vitoria-ba, atletico→??? bare 'atletico' never appears alone... 'Atlético-MG' tokens [atletico, mg]: strip → 'atletico' ∈ AMBIGUOUS → keep 'atletico-mg' ✓. 'Atletico Goianiense' → not tagged, 'atletico goianiense' via alias → atletico-go ✓. 'Atlético Acreano' → [atletico, acreano] no tag → 'atletico acreano' stays as own id ✓ (distinct from atletico-ac? there's no other atletico-ac).\n\nWait, but that breaks 'flamengo-rj' → strip 'rj' → 'flamengo' — flamengo not in AMBIGUOUS → id 'flamengo' ✓ good.\n'America-MG' → 'america mg' → strip 'mg' → 'america' ∈ AMBIGUOUS → keep 'america-mg' ✓.\n'America RN' → 'america-rn' ✓.\n'EC Bahia' → 'ec bahia' → alias (I list 'ec bahia') → 'bahia' ✓.\n'Fortaleza FC' → 'fortaleza fc' → alias → 'fortaleza' ✓ (or generic: no tag; 'fortaleza fc' — hmm need alias or suffix stripping of 'fc'/'ec'/'sc'/'ac'/'ca'? I could strip football-club tokens: ec, fc, sc, ac, ca, aa? 'EC Bahia'→'bahia' ✓, 'Fortaleza FC'→'fortaleza' ✓, 'ASA AL'→'asa-al'... 'CRB' stays. Stripping club-legal-suffix tokens generically: 'Bahia de Feira' unaffected. 'Sport Club do Recife' → strip 'club'/'do'? My alias covers it. Generic suffix stripping: tokens ∈ {ec, fc, sc, ac, ca, cb, aa, sd, im, ec?} at END? 'Fortaleza FC' ends with fc → strip → 'fortaleza'. 'Sao Paulo FC' → 'sao paulo' ✓. But 'SC Internacional' — sc at START. Strip sc/ec/fc anywhere? 'EC Vitória' → 'vitoria' → AMBIGUOUS bare → default → 'vitoria-ba' ✓ (matches BR-Football usage). Hmm but is BR-Football 'EC Vitoria' really Vitória-BA? Earlier: 'EC Vitoria' appears in Copa do Brasil 2017/2018 — plausibly Vitória-BA. And 'Vitoria EC' in Copa 2020-2022 — also Vitória-BA probably. I'll alias both → vitoria-ba.\n\nAMBIGUOUS set (bases with multiple state-variants in the data): botafogo, america, vitoria, santos, nacional, guarani, atletico, athletic? no... internacional? ('Internacional-RS' vs bare 'Internacional' vs 'Internacional' Limeira?? 'Inter de Limeira' — different name, no clash), gremio? ('Gremio-RS' vs 'Gremio' vs 'Gremio Novorizontino' — multiword distinct; bare 'gremio' unique → strip rs → 'gremio' ✓ not ambiguous), cuiaba ('Cuiaba-MT' vs bare → strip → 'cuiaba' fine), csa ('Csa-AL' → 'csa' fine).\n\nSo AMBIGUOUS = {botafogo, america, vitoria, santos, nacional, atletico, guarani, river plate? (country-tagged), tolima? no...}. Also for foreign: 'Barcelona-EQU' — 'barcelona' + 'equ' country tag — keep 'barcelona-equ' always (tag ≠ UF, country tags always kept). ✓ 'Nacional (URU)' → 'nacional uru' → tag 'uru' → 'nacional-uru' ✓. 'Nacional (PAR)' → 'nacional-par' ✓. Bare 'Nacional' (if appears in Brazilian files, e.g. 'Nacional-AM') → 'nacional-am' or 'nacional'...\n\nCountry tags list (3-letter): URU, PAR, EQU, PER, VEN, ARG, BOL, CHI, COL, MEX, ECU. Let me extract from data to be sure.\n\nDEFAULTS for bare ambiguous: botafogo→botafogo-rj, america→america-mg, vitoria→vitoria-ba, santos→santos, atletico→?? (never bare), nacional→nacional-uru? (bare 'Nacional' in Libertadores = Uruguayan Nacional probably) — hmm, risky; leave bare 'nacional' as-is (no default) unless data shows bare 'Nacional'. Let me check Libertadores list: 'Nacional (PAR)', 'Nacional (URU)', 'Nacional-URU' — no bare. OK no default needed.\n\nAlso within-Brasileirao clubs that appear with suffix in one file, bare in another, NON-ambiguous — handled by stripping. E.g. 'Ceara-CE' → 'ceara' ✓ = bare 'Ceara' ✓. 'Sport-PE' → 'sport'... wait 'Sport-PE' tokens [sport, pe] → strip 'pe' → 'sport'. Is 'sport' ambiguous? 'Sport Boys' (Peruvian, Libertadores 'Sport Boys'), 'Sporting Cristal', 'Spor