{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788281040218,"sessionID":"ses_fa22e85f8ffeHYTJ3TNp22RZ2x","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"edit","callID":"chatcmpl-tool-99611be0d955048c","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-tfe1ts5p/retort-a725f4ae3f5d/brazilian_soccer_mcp/normalize.py","newString":"def parse_date(raw: str) -> Optional[date]:\n    \"\"\"Parse the date formats present in the datasets.\n\n    Handles ISO dates (\"2023-09-24\"), ISO datetimes (\"2012-05-19 18:30:00\")\n    and Brazilian format (\"29/03/2003\").  Returns None for blank/NA values.\n    \"\"\"\n    parsed = parse_datetime(raw)\n    return parsed.date() if parsed else None\n\n\ndef parse_datetime(raw: str) -> Optional[datetime]:\n    \"\"\"Parse a dataset timestamp into a datetime, keeping the time part.\"\"\"\n    if not raw:\n        return None\n    text = raw.strip()\n    if not text or text.upper() in {\"NA\", \"N/A\", \"-\"}:\n        return None\n    for fmt in _DATE_FORMATS:\n        try:\n            return datetime.strptime(text, fmt)\n        except ValueError:\n            continue\n    return None","oldString":"def parse_date(raw: str) -> Optional[date]:\n    \"\"\"Parse the date formats present in the datasets.\n\n    Handles ISO dates (\"2023-09-24\"), ISO datetimes (\"2012-05-19 18:30:00\")\n    and Brazilian format (\"29/03/2003\").  Returns None for blank/NA values.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not raw:\n        return None\n    text = raw.strip()\n    if not text or text.upper() in {\"NA\", \"N/A\", \"-\"}:\n        return None\n    for fmt in _DATE_FORMATS:\n        try:\n            return datetime.strptime(text, fmt).date()\n        except ValueError:\n            continue\n    return None"},"output":"Edit applied successfully.","metadata":{"diagnostics":{},"diff":"Index: /Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-tfe1ts5p/retort-a725f4ae3f5d/brazilian_soccer_mcp/normalize.py\n===================================================================\n--- /Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-tfe1ts5p/retort-a725f4ae3f5d/brazilian_soccer_mcp/normalize.py\n+++ /Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-tfe1ts5p/retort-a725f4ae3f5d/brazilian_soccer_mcp/normalize.py\n@@ -371,16 +371,22 @@\n \n     Handles ISO dates (\"2023-09-24\"), ISO datetimes (\"2012-05-19 18:30:00\")\n     and Brazilian format (\"29/03/2003\").  Returns None for blank/NA values.\n     \"\"\"\n+    parsed = parse_datetime(raw)\n+    return parsed.date() if parsed else None\n+\n+\n+def parse_datetime(raw: str) -> Optional[datetime]:\n+    \"\"\"Parse a dataset timestamp into a datetime, keeping the time part.\"\"\"\n     if not raw:\n         return None\n     text = raw.strip()\n     if not text or text.upper() in {\"NA\", \"N/A\", \"-\"}:\n         return None\n     for fmt in _DATE_FORMATS:\n         try:\n-            return datetime.strptime(text, fmt).date()\n+            return datetime.strptime(text, fmt)\n         except ValueError:\n             continue\n     return None\n \n","filediff":{"file":"/Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-tfe1ts5p/retort-a725f4ae3f5d/brazilian_soccer_mcp/normalize.py","patch":"Index: /Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-tfe1ts5p/retort-a725f4ae3f5d/brazilian_soccer_mcp/normalize.py\n===================================================================\n--- /Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-tfe1ts5p/retort-a725f4ae3f5d/brazilian_soccer_mcp/normalize.py\n+++ /Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-tfe1ts5p/retort-a725f4ae3f5d/brazilian_soccer_mcp/normalize.py\n@@ -371,16 +371,22 @@\n \n     Handles ISO dates (\"2023-09-24\"), ISO datetimes (\"2012-05-19 18:30:00\")\n     and Brazilian format (\"29/03/2003\").  Returns None for blank/NA values.\n     \"\"\"\n+    parsed = parse_datetime(raw)\n+    return parsed.date() if parsed else None\n+\n+\n+def parse_datetime(raw: str) -> Optional[datetime]:\n+    \"\"\"Parse a dataset timestamp into a datetime, keeping the time part.\"\"\"\n     if not raw:\n         return None\n     text = raw.strip()\n     if not text or text.upper() in {\"NA\", \"N/A\", \"-\"}:\n         return None\n     for fmt in _DATE_FORMATS:\n         try:\n-            return datetime.strptime(text, fmt).date()\n+            return datetime.strptime(text, fmt)\n         except ValueError:\n             continue\n     return None\n \n","additions":7,"deletions":1},"truncated":false},"title":"brazilian_soccer_mcp/normalize.py","time":{"start":1788281040216,"end":1788281040217}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"Wait — there's a design tension I need to resolve: `Match.home_team` now stores DISPLAY names (e.g. \"Flamengo\", \"Athletico Paranaense\"), but `resolve_team` and club resolution work off display names too. The service layer will match on display names. Since display names are derived deterministically from canonical ids, two datasets' variants of the same club produce the same display name ✓. That's consistent.\n\nBut `normalize_team_id` on a display name should round-trip: normalize(\"Athletico Paranaense\") → 'athletico paranaense' → alias → 'athletico-pr' ✓. normalize(\"Red Bull Bragantino\") → 'red bull bragantino' → alias → 'bragantino' ✓. normalize(\"Atlético Mineiro\") → 'atletico mineiro' → alias → 'atletico-mg' ✓. Good — round trips work.\n\n`resolve_club_players`: FIFA clubs like 'Grêmio' (display in FIFA is 'Grêmio'). normalize_team_id('Grêmio') → 'gremio'. teams_by... players_by_club keys casefolded 'grêmio'. candidates: resolved team (from match data 'Grêmio') casefold 'grêmio' ✓ matches. Also normalize_team_id(club_key) — club_key 'grêmio' → normalize → 'gremio' == canonical_id 'gremio' ✓. Good.\n\nFor FIFA club 'América FC (Minas Gerais)': players_by_club key 'américa fc (minas gerais)'. Query 'América-MG' → canonical 'america-mg'; normalize_team_id(club_key) = 'america-mg' ✓ match. \n\nNote: resolve_team searches known_teams (match teams + FIFA clubs). Query 'América-MG' — known_teams has 'América Mineiro' (display). normalize('América-MG') → 'america-mg' → display 'América Mineiro' ✓ found.\n\nOne issue: `known_teams` includes FIFA club names like 'FC Barcelona', 'Liverpool'. resolve_team('Barcelona') — in match data (Libertadores) 'Barcelona (EQU)'... query 'Barcelona' → exact? known_teams has 'fc barcelona' not 'barcelona'. startsWith 'barcelona'? 'barcelona (equ)' ✓ → returns Barcelona (EQU). Hmm — questionable for \"Which players play at Barcelona?\" (FIFA FC Barcelona) — resolve_team returns match-team first. But resolve_club_players handles players separately ✓. Fine.\n\nAlso 'time' for Brasileirao: I extract HH:MM from datetime. parse_date returns date — TIME LOST! parse_date('2012-05-19 18:30:00') → date(2012,5,19). The time is dropped. I use match_date.strftime(\"%H:%M\") — date has no time → \"00:00\"!! BUG: date objects' strftime %H:%M gives 00:00. I need parse to keep datetime. Let me fix: add a `parse_datetime` helper or in loader parse datetime separately with str split. Simplest: in loader, extract time from the raw string via regex/split on space. Let me fix: for Brasileirao/cup/libertadores rows, datetime strings are 'YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM:SS' → time = part after space truncated to HH:MM.\n\nActually cleaner: add `parse_datetime(raw) -> Optional[datetime]` in normalize.py and use `.date()` and `.strftime('%H:%M')`. Let me update normalize.py and loader.py accordingly.\n\nAlso in _load_br_football, time is '20:00:00' → keep as '20:00'? I set time=row['time'] raw '20:00:00'. Normalize to HH:MM: strip seconds. Let me make a small helper `_hhmm(text)`.\n\nLet me fix these now.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_05ddb2708001q3wlvsPjrGudZV","sessionID":"ses_fa22e85f8ffeHYTJ3TNp22RZ2x","messageID":"msg_05ddaf7da001EUw04py4UUNOie"}}
