p file has 92/108 played (85%) → skipped → br_football 111/111 chosen. That's actually good behavior (br has complete scores for 2021), though it loses round labels. Trade-off is fine — scores matter more than round labels. But hmm, the 2021 cup file had 108 rows with 16 unplayed... The cup data 2021 might be truncated. br_football 2021 has 111 (round info lost). It's a reasonable choice.\n\nAlso note: 2020 cup final legs were played in Feb-Mar 2021 — my cup season attribution uses date year! BR-Football cup rows dated 2021-02-28 ('Grêmio 0-1 Palmeiras (Copa do Brasil Final)') → season 2021?! But they belong to the 2020 cup! Wait — the printed 2020 finals above came from the CUP file (which has explicit season 2020 for those Feb 2021 dates ✓). But in BR-Football, those same matches are dated 2021-02-28/2021-03-07 → assigned season 2021. For the cup file primary (2020) it's fine. But for BR-Football cup rows in Jan-Feb — 2020 cup rounds also ran into early 2021 (semifinals Dec 30, finals Feb/Mar). Since the cup file is primary for 2020, no impact on primary view. For search across all sources, minor misattribution in the non-primary br rows — acceptable.\n\nWait, actually — there's a subtlety: BR-Football Copa do Brasil 2021 = 111 matches (dated 2021). Are the Feb/Mar 2021 cup matches (2020 finals) INCLUDED in that 111? Then br 'cup 2021' = 111 includes ~6 late-2020 matches + 2021 season matches. But since primary for 2021 is br (111 rows), the primary 2021 cup view includes those final legs of the 2020 cup misattributed to 2021. Hmm. Does that break anything? find_finals(2021) would show the 2020 finals under 2021... The BDD tests: I'll test find_finals for Copa do Brasil 2013 (Flamengo champion!) or Libertadores 2019/2020 — solid.\n\nShould I apply the Jan/Feb → previous-year rule to cup matches too? The 2020 cup DID end in March 2021. But normally (2012-2019) the cup runs Feb/Mar-Nov with finals Oct/Nov — only the COVID 2020 edition spilled into Feb/Mar 2021. If I apply Jan/Feb→prev-year to cups: 2021 Feb/Mar cup matches → 2020 ✓ correct for COVID years; but any normal-year February first-round matches (e.g. 2019 cup first round Feb 2019) → misattributed to 2018!! The cup STARTS in February typically. So a blanket Jan/Feb rule for cups is wrong. March rule? 2020 finals were Feb 28 and Mar 7. Cup first rounds in normal years start ~Feb 10-Mar. No clean rule.\n\nAlternative: for BR-Football cup rows, if a match is in Jan/Feb/early-March AND its pair (home,away) appears in a completed later stage... too complex. Since the dedicated cup file handles 2012-2020 correctly (explicit seasons) and is primary for those years, and br_football primary only for 2021-2023 where attribution is calendar-year correct (2021 cup ran May-June... wait no — 2021 Copa do Brasil ran from March to October 2021, finals Oct 2021 — and br's 111 '2021' rows include the Feb/Mar 2021 legs of the 2020 final (6 legs: 2 final + 4 semi? Dec 30 semifinal too). Hmm.\n\nLet me quantify: br cup rows dated Jan-Mar 2021: semis Dec 30 2020 (2), finals Feb 28 & Mar 7 (2) → those 4-6 matches belong to the 2020 cup. They'd appear under 2021. It's ~5% of 111 rows. Impact: find_finals('Copa do Brasil', 2021) shows the 2020 final as a 2021 final — WRONG-ish.\n\nFix: for cup competitions, when month is Jan/Feb/Mar AND the previous calendar year's edition of the same pair-fixture exists... still complex. Simpler heuristic: apply the Jan-Feb rule to cups too? Normal years: 2014-2019 cup first rounds: check months. If normal-year cup first rounds are never before March, applying Jan-Feb→prev-year to cups is safe and fixes the COVID spillover. Let me check month distribution of cup matches in br_football for non-COVID years.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_05de1f274001pTwBpawHgGaXMZ","sessionID":"ses_fa22e85f8ffeHYTJ3TNp22RZ2x","messageID":"msg_05de1b6fd001oInvy2NrcCHrfF"}}
