{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788281552169,"sessionID":"ses_fa22e85f8ffeHYTJ3TNp22RZ2x","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"bash","callID":"chatcmpl-tool-8fa16af64364a70e","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"source venv/bin/activate && python << 'EOF'\nimport asyncio\nfrom brazilian_soccer_mcp.loader import SoccerData\nimport brazilian_soccer_mcp.server as srv\n\ndata = SoccerData.load()\nserver = srv.build_server(data)\n\nasync def run():\n    try:\n        await server.call_tool('nonexistent_tool', {})\n    except Exception as e:\n        print('unknown tool ->', type(e).__name__, ':', str(e)[:80])\n    try:\n        await server.call_tool('team_record', {'team': 'Not A Real Team FC'})\n    except Exception as e:\n        print('bad team ->', type(e).__name__, ':', str(e)[:100])\n    # bad args\n    try:\n        await server.call_tool('standings', {'competition': 'Fake Comp', 'season': 2019})\n    except Exception as e:\n        print('bad comp ->', type(e).__name__, ':', str(e)[:100])\n\nasyncio.run(run())\nEOF","workdir":"/Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-tfe1ts5p/retort-a725f4ae3f5d"},"output":"unknown tool -> ToolError : Unknown tool: nonexistent_tool\nbad team -> UnexpectedToolError : Error executing tool team_record\nbad comp -> UnexpectedToolError : Error executing tool standings\n","metadata":{"output":"unknown tool -> ToolError : Unknown tool: nonexistent_tool\nbad team -> UnexpectedToolError : Error executing tool team_record\nbad comp -> UnexpectedToolError : Error executing tool standings\n","exit":0,"truncated":false},"title":"source venv/bin/activate && python << 'EOF'\nimport asyncio\nfrom brazilian_soccer_mcp.loader import SoccerData\nimport brazilian_soccer_mcp.server as srv\n\ndata = SoccerData.load()\nserver = srv.build_server(data)\n\nasync def run():\n    try:\n        await server.call_tool('nonexistent_tool', {})\n    except Exception as e:\n        print('unknown tool ->', type(e).__name__, ':', str(e)[:80])\n    try:\n        await server.call_tool('team_record', {'team': 'Not A Real Team FC'})\n    except Exception as e:\n        print('bad team ->', type(e).__name__, ':', str(e)[:100])\n    # bad args\n    try:\n        await server.call_tool('standings', {'competition': 'Fake Comp', 'season': 2019})\n    except Exception as e:\n        print('bad comp ->', type(e).__name__, ':', str(e)[:100])\n\nasyncio.run(run())\nEOF","time":{"start":1788281552074,"end":1788281552167}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"All facts gathered. One oddity: 'Lib 2020' final shows date 2020-01-30 — the Palmeiras 1-0 Santos final was actually 2021-01-30 (COVID-delayed 2020 edition final played Jan 30, 2021!). The dataset has it as 2020-01-30 — hmm, either the dataset has a date error or it's the actual 2020 season final recorded with a 2020 date. The real match: 2021-01-30, Palmeiras 1-0 Santos at Maracanã. Dataset says 2020-01-30 — the dataset's date is wrong by one year (but season 2020 ✓). Not my problem — data as provided. The final query works: season 2020 final = Palmeiras 1-0 Santos ✓ correct teams/result.\n\nAlso interesting: Flamengo Sep 2023 shows Copa do Brasil matches (São Paulo 1-1 Flamengo 2023-09-24) — real (2023 cup semis). \n\nJosué Chiamulera 83 top Grêmio player? Hmm — Grêmio 2018 squad... FIFA19 had 'Luan' 83? Whatever the data says; we assert average and count (20 players) rather than specific names... Actually let me assert count=20 and avg rating = 73.3 (deterministic).\n\nSantos STs: 'Luimo Boas Santos' etc. — data's minor misspellings, fine.\n\nNow let me also double check: search_players(name='Gabriel Barbosa') → empty (data doesn't have him). For BDD test on \"Who is Gabriel Barbosa?\" the expected behavior = search by name → empty result set (not crash). I'll test that it returns 0 players gracefully.\n\nNow write the test suite. Structure (BDD GWT):\n\ntests/conftest.py:\n```python\nimport pytest\nfrom brazilian_soccer_mcp.loader import SoccerData\nfrom brazilian_soccer_mcp.service import SoccerQueryService\n\n@pytest.fixture(scope=\"session\")\ndef data(): return SoccerData.load()\n\n@pytest.fixture(scope=\"session\")\ndef service(data): return SoccerQueryService(data)\n```\nPlus an event_loop for async server tests? I'll use asyncio.run inside sync tests — no pytest-asyncio needed. But server fixture: build_server(data) — creating MCPServer is cheap.\n\nFor each test module — Gherkin docstring at top (Feature), each test function has Scenario docstring, and body organized Given/When/Then. I'll use small helper functions or plain sections. The style: no inline comments, GWT expressed through docstring + code sections.\n\nWait — one more thing to check: `_resolve` raises ValueError for unknown team. MCP tools will surface that as tool errors — good behavior. Test that unknown team raises ValueError in service, and via server call_tool raises ToolError/UnexpectedToolError.\n\nLet me check what call_tool does with a ValueError — mcp 2.x wraps exceptions. From docstring: \"UnexpectedToolError: If the tool (or any resolver) raises anything else\". So ValueError → UnexpectedToolError raised from call_tool. I'll test with pytest.raises(Exception) or specifically UnexpectedToolError. Let me check the exception import path: mcp.server.mcpserver? Or mcp_types. Let me check quickly. Also unknown tool name → ToolError.\n\nAlso: the stdio round-trip test — spawn `python -m brazilian_soccer_mcp`, send initialize/initialized/tools-list/tools-call. That test proves \"server builds and runs\". \n\nLet me now check the error classes.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_05de2f1940016lZW42ai3EpC43","sessionID":"ses_fa22e85f8ffeHYTJ3TNp22RZ2x","messageID":"msg_05de2b6e0001XJ7QXZe8rQnwcC"}}
