teria, maybe add a pytest.ini? Not needed.\n4. Also double check: the spec says \"At least 20 sample questions can be answered\" — I'll document 20+ sample questions in README mapped to tools.\n5. Verify `python -m brazilian_soccer_mcp --help`? No — it runs the server (blocking). The stdio test covers it.\n\nLet me also run a quick lint-ish check (python -m compileall / pyflakes not installed). I can at least ensure all modules import cleanly and check for unused imports quickly. Let me run python -m py_compile on all files and a quick import check. Also run the full test suite once more with -p no:cacheprovider to be sure, and verify git status to see what's changed.\n\nFor README — rewrite with: overview, quick start, MCP config example (claude_desktop_config / opencode), tools table, sample questions (20+), testing instructions, data sources & licenses, architecture notes (normalization, dedup).\n\nLet me write the README now.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_05de88b45001Ia8YmSmNB4VNYf","sessionID":"ses_fa22e85f8ffeHYTJ3TNp22RZ2x","messageID":"msg_05de8669700124ZmbLiPKhEBTm"}}
