{"type":"text","timestamp":1788282060914,"sessionID":"ses_fa22e85f8ffeHYTJ3TNp22RZ2x","part":{"id":"prt_05dea9e80001pAFxFcE2sw6zRO","messageID":"msg_05dea91fe001u2DBiwl9LX0bw3","sessionID":"ses_fa22e85f8ffeHYTJ3TNp22RZ2x","type":"text","text":"Implemented per TASK.md: a Brazilian soccer MCP server in `brazilian_soccer_mcp/` (7 modules) with an 18-tool MCP server (`python -m brazilian_soccer_mcp`), plus a BDD GWT pytest suite in `tests/` — **88/88 tests pass in ~4s**, pyflakes clean.\n\nKey design points:\n- **Normalization** (`normalize.py`): alias table + state/country-tag rules unify every spelling (\"Palmeiras-SP\"/\"Palmeiras\", \"Atletico-PR\"/\"Athletico Paranaense\"/\"Athletico\", FIFA's \"América FC (Minas Gerais)\") while keeping genuinely ambiguous clubs distinct (Botafogo-RJ vs -PB); parses all 3 date formats; UTF-8 throughout.\n- **Loader** (`loader.py`): all 6 CSVs load into 23,954 matches + 18,207 players, with a de-duplicated \"primary\" view per (competition, season) — correct team counts per season (24/24/22/20...), COVID-era Jan/Feb matches attributed to the prior season, and BR-Football corner/shot/attack stats joined cross-file onto primary matches.\n- **Validation**: computed standings reproduce all 20 real Série A champions 2003–2022 (2019 Flamengo: 90 pts, 28W-6D-4L — matching the spec's example) and real relegated teams.\n- **Performance**: queries answer in 1–20 ms (budgets: <2s simple, <5s aggregate); data load ≈1s.\n- **MCP**: verified end-to-end over stdio JSON-RPC (initialize → tools/list → tools/call) in the test suite; tools cover match/team/player/competition/statistics queries, including 24 documented sample questions.","time":{"start":1788282052224,"end":1788282060911}}}
